@startuml supervisor_installation
hide empty description
title Permanent supervisor installation and admitted work
state "Installation" as installation {
  [*] --> Prepared
  Prepared --> Applied : Landlock then Seccomp\npublish irreversible stage
  Applied --> Transferred : sole listener owner sends SCM_RIGHTS
  Transferred --> Ready : ready/proceed within original budget
  Ready --> Failed : reactor death / listener failure
  Prepared --> Failed : acquisition failure
  Applied --> Failed : timeout or transport failure\nretain applied stage
  Transferred --> Failed : invalid handshake / timeout
  Failed --> Retired : retire owned resources\nfilter remains installed
  Ready --> Retired : owner/session termination
}
state "Per-notification work" as work {
  [*] --> Admission
  Admission --> Rejected : total >= 128 or TID >= 8\none EAGAIN attempt
  Admission --> Helper : acquire counted lease
  Helper --> Decision : bounded identity-bound snapshot
  Decision --> Helper : validated JVM verdict\nexecute operation
  Helper --> Reply : terminal owned result
  Reply --> Released : reactor claims sole reply
  Helper --> Cancelled : deadline / teardown
  Decision --> Cancelled : deadline / teardown
  Cancelled --> Released : cancel + reap + late FD disposal
  Rejected --> [*]
  Released --> [*] : release counted lease once
}
Ready --> Admission : task registration lease
note bottom of installation
  One monotonic 30s handshake deadline (validated lower override).
  Callback publication completes only after callback returns/throws.
  Permanent state cannot be rolled back.
  Failed listener health rejects new registrations.
end note
note right of Helper
  Default: 4 active / 64 queued helper jobs.
  Pinned proc/pidfd and typed root/dirfd capabilities.
  Exact owned-descriptor handoff through private IPC.
  Reuse slot only after previous child is reaped.
end note
@enduml
